# remotefs settings: shipped by stack/remotefs. Every setting remotefs reads.
#
# This machine's values go in ~/.config/remotefs/remotefs.local.env, beside this file (yours, never
# shipped). The environment wins over both: `REMOTEFS_MOUNT_TIMEOUT=60 remotefs mount nas` does
# what it says. Format: NAME=value, one per line, read and never sourced (only a leading ~/, or a
# value that is ~, is expanded, to $HOME; a value may be quoted). A commented line is the default
# used when nothing sets it. `remotefs config` is to list and set them; until it exists, edit
# remotefs.local.env.

# Where a mount goes when its entry names no mountpoint: <here>/<label>
#REMOTEFS_MOUNT_HOME=~/mnt
# What every mount gets unless its entry says `defaults: false`
#REMOTEFS_DEFAULT_OPTIONS="reconnect ServerAliveInterval=15 ServerAliveCountMax=3"
# The sshfs to run
#REMOTEFS_SSHFS=sshfs
# Seconds: the ssh check before a mount, sshfs itself, and asking a mount whether it answers
#REMOTEFS_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=5
#REMOTEFS_MOUNT_TIMEOUT=20
#REMOTEFS_STAT_TIMEOUT=3
